  "title": "How to Work with Vectors",
  "content": "<p>A <strong>vector</strong> has magnitude and direction. Written as \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) (bold) or \\(\\vec{AB}\\) or column vector \\(\\binom{x}{y}\\).</p><p><strong>Adding vectors:</strong> \\(\\binom{a}{b} + \\binom{c}{d} = \\binom{a+c}{b+d}\\). <strong>Subtracting:</strong> reverse the second and add.</p><p><strong>Scalar multiplication:</strong> \\(k\\binom{a}{b} = \\binom{ka}{kb}\\)</p><p>To go from A to B: \\(\\vec{AB} = \\mathbf{b} - \\mathbf{a}\\) (where \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) are position vectors from the origin).</p><p><strong>Parallel vectors:</strong> \\(\\mathbf{p}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{q}\\) are parallel if \\(\\mathbf{p} = k\\mathbf{q}\\) for some scalar \\(k\\).</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>If \\(\\vec{OA} = \\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\vec{OB} = \\mathbf{b}\\), find \\(\\vec{AB}\\).</strong></p><p>\\(\\vec{AB} = \\vec{AO} + \\vec{OB} = -\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{b} - \\mathbf{a}\\)</p>"
 },
